/*  Interfaces, and the modules and books a program pulls.

    ★ MONOMORPHIZED, as in C# (`CodeGenerator.Types.cs`, "Interfaces — MONOMORPHIZATION"): an
      interface stands in exactly one place, a function's parameter, and at every call the argument
      is a concrete object. So a function taking an interface is never built as it is written — each
      call asks for a copy in which the parameter is the object passed, and the copies are built once
      the program is, until no copy asks for another. A default written `unto` an interface arrives
      already copied onto each conformer that lacks one: the checker does that.

    ★ A module or a book is an object, usually of no fields; `Pull a shapes.` makes one, named for
      it, for the length of the pull, and `shapes's origin` is a method called on it.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// A name as C: every character but an ASCII letter or digit becomes an underscore — a
    /// hyphen, the spaces of a name the loader renamed (`point in shapes`), the slashes of a
    /// folder's (`helper in top/lib`), and the commas of a version dispatch made
    /// (`check given text literal, wants number`).
    Bind text to c-ident, given (the text name):
        Define letters as a chase.
        Insert name into letters.
        Define cleaned as a chase.
        Define place as 1.
        While place is not greater than the number of letters, repeat:
            Define ch as item place of letters.
            If "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789" contains ch, insert ch into cleaned.
            Otherwise, insert "_" into cleaned.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        Return cleaned converted to text.
    Done.

    /// What an object conforms to that this compiler cannot build yet, or "".
    Bind text to conformance-beyond unto emitter, given (the node definition):
        For each conformed in (cast field-of on (definition, 8))'s children, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (conformed).
            If name is "region", return "an object that is a region".
            If name is not "module" and name is not "book" and (the entry for name in one's interfaces) is void:
                Return "an object conforming to '{name}'".
            Done.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Whether a function takes an interface anywhere — and so is built only as its copies.
    Bind fact or failure to takes-interface unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If taken starts with "interface ", return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// The copy of `called` this call needs: its C name, asked for if it has not been yet. Each
    /// interface parameter takes the kind of the object passed in its place.
    Bind text or failure to c-specialized-name unto emitter, given (the node called, the node call):
        Define function-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (called, 1)).
        Define handed as (cast field-of on (call, 2))'s children.
        Define c-named as cast c-function-name on (function-name).
        Define overrides as a map from text to text.
        Define place as 0.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (called, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define taken as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If taken starts with "interface ":
                Define passed as cast one's kind-of on (item place of handed) or pass the failure off.
                Define object-name as cast object-of on (passed).
                If object-name is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a {passed} passed for an interface")).
                The c-named becomes "{c-named}__{cast c-ident on (object-name)}".
                In overrides, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)) becomes passed.
            Done.
        Done.
        If (the entry for c-named in one's specialized) is void:
            In one's specialized, the entry for c-named becomes true.
            Insert called into one's pending-functions.
            Insert c-named into one's pending-names.
            Insert overrides into one's pending-kinds.
        Done.
        Return c-named.
    Done.

    /// `cast area on one` — a method called with what it is called on as its first argument.
    Bind node or failure to method-by-argument unto emitter, given (the node call):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (call, 1).
        If callee's kind is not "VariableReference", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of a {callee's kind}")).
        Define handed as (cast field-of on (call, 2))'s children.
        If the number of handed is 0, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of something other than the program's own function")).
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of handed) or pass the failure off.
        Define object-name as cast object-of on (held).
        Define method as the entry for "{object-name}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1))}" in one's methods.
        If object-name is "" or method is void:
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a call of something other than the program's own function")).
        Done.
        Return method.
    Done.

    /// The same call written as `<first argument>'s <method> on (<the rest>)`.
    Bind node to as-method-call, given (the node call):
        Define handed as (cast field-of on (call, 2))'s children.
        Define rest as cast listed.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in handed, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than 1, cast rest's add on (argument).
        Done.
        Define reached as cast made on ("PossessiveAccess", a series with (item 1 of handed, cast field-of on (cast field-of on (call, 1), 1))).
        Return cast made on ("CastExpression", a series with (reached, rest)).
    Done.

    /// The module or book objects a pull names, each made for its length under its name.
    Bind void or failure to emit-pulled-modules unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        For each pulled in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define pulled-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pulled, 1)).
            If (the entry for pulled-name in one's objects) is not void:
                Define known-as as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pulled, 2)).
                Define type-c as cast c-struct-name on (pulled-name).
                Cast one's line on ("{type-c} {cast c-name on (known-as)} = ({type-c})\{ 0 \};").
                In one's kinds, the entry for known-as becomes "object {pulled-name}".
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
